# playpick cell: mode=walk boss=saved spec=druid:balance style=flee
# size=10 difficulty=normal view=844x390,touch save=carried (behaves as
# fresh, #273 -- carried never actually carries across separate playbot
# invocations because the dev-server port is derived from the process
# pid). `boss=saved` is a coverage label only (direction.md's 2026-09-25
# note on playpick.ts): a mode=walk evening steers at no named boss, the
# walk starts at the door same as any other, and the fresh/carried default
# is already 10-normal, so no #hash unlock is needed to reach this cell.
#
# What is new here: checked sessions.jsonl -- druid:balance has been
# played four times before (2026-09-25 daily, 2026-09-26/09-27
# battleground x2, 2026-09-28 daily) and never once inside mode=walk or
# mode=clear, so this is the first evening this spec has ever walked.
# It is also only the third flee-style #271 confirmation on record, and
# the first to put flee on a ranged caster dps rather than a healer
# (paladin:holy, ninth confirmation) or a hunter (seventh). druid's own
# moveSpeed is 167 (src/sim/classes.ts:618) -- squarely between the
# confirmed-slow tier (158: warrior/paladin/priest/warlock, all stall/wipe
# THE VIGIL) and the one confirmed-fast clean crossing (rogue, 178) --
# so this is also a new data point on whether VIGIL's watchmen catch
# everything below rogue's own speed, or whether 167 is fast enough to
# get through where 158 is not (hunter's 173 flee reading crossed clean
# per the eighth #271 confirmation, so if druid also crosses clean this
# starts drawing the actual speed line rather than a flat "slow tier
# dies, fast tier lives").
#
# If it crosses THE VIGIL, the evening keeps running (8 fights, 300s
# budget) rather than stopping at the first room -- direction.md's #3
# hypothesis has eleven confirmations of the PULL AGAIN retry bug and all
# eleven happened inside THE VIGIL specifically; nobody has yet gotten a
# travel-mode wipe in a *different* corridor to see whether the same bug
# reproduces there or is actually specific to this one room. A clean
# VIGIL crossing here is the first real chance at that.
